      ":question/id": "2737bc55-42bf-5b9f-a99a-930a65660299",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-348643",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $r(t)=\u27e8t+4,\\,\\frac{3t+1}{t}\u27e9,$ calculate $r(3).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$r(3)=\u27e8$\n{{field-1}} $,$\n\n{{field-2}}$\u27e9$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We substitute $t=3$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =\u27e83+4,\\,\\frac{3(3)+1}{3}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e87,\\,\\frac{10}{3}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
